# Phase 8: per-note velocity, length and channel (the matrix's rows 3-5,
# seq_submit_track_ex()). A note is P:D:V:L:C; - is the track's setting.
#
# Velocity: the note's own times the track's velocity / 100, rounded,
# kept to 1..127. At the default 100 it plays as written; - is the
# track's velocity itself.
open virtual
track 1 60:1:80 62:1:- 64:1:127 65:1:1
play continue
runto 4
log
# track velocity 50: 80 -> 40, - -> 50, 127 -> 64 (63.5 rounds up),
# 1 -> 1 (0.5 rounds up; never 0, which would be a note-off)
vel 1 = 50
runto 8
log
# track velocity 127: 80 -> 102 (101.6), 127 -> 127 (161, kept to 127)
vel 1 = 127
runto 12
log
close
#
# Length: the note-off comes that long after the note-on, rounded to a
# tick; a length longer than the step is shortened to it (62: 2 beats
# in a 1-beat step, so as before, off where 64 starts); one tick is the
# shortest (65). - is the whole step, as always.
open virtual
track 1 60:1:-:1/2 62:1:-:2 64:1:-:- 65:1/2:-:1/2520 r:1/2:-:7
play continue
runto 4
log
state
close
#
# Channel: per note, for that note only. The track's channel (1) is
# what the state shows. Track 2 sounds 60 on channel 5 for 2 beats;
# track 1's 60 on channel 5 is a re-strike, and its note-off doesn't
# cut track 2's note: the off goes out only when both have ended.
open virtual
track 2:5 60:2
track 1 60:1:-:-:5 62:1:-:-:- r:1
play continue
runto 3
log
state
close
#
# Errors, nothing changed: velocity 0 or 128, length 0, under a tick,
# or negative other than -1, channel 0 or 17. Rests aren't looked at,
# whatever their extra fields hold.
open virtual
track 1 60:1:0
track 1 60:1:128
track 1 60:1:-:0
track 1 60:1:-:1/5040
track 1 60:1:-:-2
track 1 60:1:-:-:0
track 1 60:1:-:-:17
track 1 r:1:0:0:99 60:1:90:1/2:16
play continue
runto 2
log
close
